    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Frederick Mauck filed the original town plat on May 7, 1827, naming the settlement Mauck’s Port after his family.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        3,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/mauckport_indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1847 citizens petitioned to rename Mauckport New Market, but the change reversed in 1850 because of a postal conflict.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        28,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/mauckport_indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "John Peter Mauck operated Indiana’s first ferry, a raft and tow line crossing from Mauckport to Brandenburg, Kentucky, as early as 1808.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mauckport%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Daniel Boone’s brother, Squire Boone, explored the area and settled near Mauckport in 1806, leaving his remains in nearby caverns.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        14,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/mauckport_indiana",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Mauckport’s wharf became a frequent stop for steam ships and river barges, the closest Ohio River port to Corydon, the state’s first capital.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mauckport%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Confederate General John Hunt Morgan and his troops once tried to cross the Ohio River into Indiana at Mauckport during the Civil War.",
